# Paint

Simple painting. Keys **1–9** pick the colour (1 black, 2 red, 3 green,
4 blue, 5 yellow, 6 magenta, 7 cyan, 8 orange, 9 white). The brush follows
the mouse and paints only while the button is held. This is the live canvas
counterpart of `examples/paint_openfl.wcn`: the WCHNT schema and painting
logic match; the Target section adapts input and drawing to the browser.

The palette is a plain data map in Construction (hex ARGB literals); colour
selection (a `switch` on the held digit), the brush update, and drawing all
live in WCHNT. Target only reads input, injects it, steps, and asks WCHNT to
paint.

## Schema

```
Paint = Canvas Palette Input Brush/brush1 Brush/brush2
Canvas = Int/width Int/height
Brush = Int/x Int/y Int/rad Int/colour Bool/painting
>Input = Int/x Int/y Bool/down Int/key
Colour = "Black" | "White" | "Red" | "Green" | "Blue" | "Yellow" | "Cyan" | "Magenta" | "Orange"
Palette = {Colour:Int}
```

## Construction

```
[:Paint
  [:Canvas 800 600]
  [:Palette
    {Colour:Int
      Black:   0xFF000000
      White:   0xFFFFFFFF
      Red:     0xFFFF0000
      Green:   0xFF00FF00
      Blue:    0xFF0000FF
      Yellow:  0xFFFFFF00
      Magenta: 0xFFFF00FF
      Cyan:    0xFF00FFFF
      Orange:  0xFFFF8000
    }
  ]
  [:Input 0 0 false 0]
  [:Brush 0 0 5 0xFF000000 false]
  [:Brush 0 0 5 0xFF000000 false]
]
```

## Methods

```
Paint::step = {
  key = input.key.
  nextColour = if (key == 0) { brush1.colour } else { palette.colourForKey(key) }.
  nextBrush1 = [:Brush input.x input.y brush1.rad nextColour input.down].
  nextBrush2 = [:Brush input.y input.x brush2.rad nextColour input.down].
  [:Paint canvas palette input nextBrush1 nextBrush2]
}

Input::update! = { [:Input x y down key] }

Palette::colourForKey = { Int/key |
  switch (key)
    1 -> { colourToInt.get(Black) }
    2 -> { colourToInt.get(Red) }
    3 -> { colourToInt.get(Green) }
    4 -> { colourToInt.get(Blue) }
    5 -> { colourToInt.get(Yellow) }
    6 -> { colourToInt.get(Magenta) }
    7 -> { colourToInt.get(Cyan) }
    8 -> { colourToInt.get(Orange) }
    else -> { colourToInt.get(White) }
}

Brush::paint = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(colour).drawCircle(x, y, rad).endFill()
}

Canvas::paint = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(0xFFFFFFFF).drawRect(0, 0, width, height).endFill()
}
```

## Target

```
%canvas

%init
var assemblage;

function init() {
    assemblage = PaintAssemblage.factory();
    assemblage.canvas.paint(wchntGraphics);
}

%step
function step() {
    var key = 0;
    for (var n = 1; n <= 9; n++) {
        if (input.keys[String(n)]) { key = n; }
    }
    var mx = Math.round(input.mouse.x * 800);
    var my = Math.round(input.mouse.y * 600);
    assemblage.input.inject(mx, my, input.mouse.down, key);
    assemblage = assemblage.step();
    if (assemblage.brush1.painting) assemblage.brush1.paint(wchntGraphics);
    if (assemblage.brush2.painting) assemblage.brush2.paint(wchntGraphics);
}
```
